cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SymCE or these results, please cite the paper."
title: "SymCE: counterexample generation against per-theorem symbolic verifiers"
abstract: >-
  A corpus of 4,707 false undergraduate algebra and real-analysis conjectures,
  each paired with an independent executable Python verifier and a witness
  schema, together with the training and evaluation pipeline used in
  "Counterexample Generation via Per-Theorem Symbolic Verifiers: When Imitation
  Hurts and Reinforcement Repairs".
